# API v1
Only binance:perpetual:BTCUSDT. GET JSON, [from,to) UTC milliseconds. Optional symbol must be BTCUSDT. Maximum raw/aggregate/OI range 4 hours; raw pages 1..1000; aggregation at most 250000 executions, 300 bars, 18000 cells, 512 cells/bar (capacity flags preserved). Errors are explicit; no fallback.
- /v1/health: DB reachability, collector freshness/retries, disk pause, metadata and OI freshness.
- /v1/capabilities: instrument, transports, limits, tickSize, retention.
- /v1/coverage?from=&to=: confirmed bounds, explicit gaps, completeness, durable aggregate ID watermark, OI status. Unrecorded/expired/current tail differs from a covered empty interval.
- /v1/executions?from=&to=&after=0&limit=1000&watermark=: ordered id > after AND id <= watermark, page nextAfter (null at end). Capture watermark on page 1; retain it for all history pages. Then /v1/live with after=cursor and a NEW watermark catches the durable tail. Inserts become visible to clients only after committed checkpoint. FINAL eliminates replay duplicates before async merges.
- /v1/footprints?from=&to=&interval=1m&rowPrice=25&watermark=: common pure client accumulator, full bounded replacement bars. Same interval and identical complete bounds reproduce values. Execution-derived OHLC and quote volume also returned. No approximate quote volume.
- /v1/execution-candles: same execution-derived projection, never native/script OHLCV.
- /v1/native-candles?interval=1m&from=: proxied native Binance klines (1000 max, 2s cache); explicitly separate source and cumulative base/actual native quote volume. Native candles are not durable executions.
- /v1/oi?from=&to=: observed samples only, sourceTimeMs, observedAtMs, value BTC, max 1000 rows and truncated flag, gaps. No historical backfill/interpolation.
- WS /v1/stream: subscribe `{type:"subscribe",version:1,after,from}` for executions, or include native `interval`. `from` must be within4h; cursor cannot exceed durable head. Server sends `{type:"executions",version:1,after,cursor,watermark,executions,coverage,collector,tickSize,sentAt}`. Rows strictly after acknowledged cursor, no more1000 per batch. ACK `{type:"ack",cursor}` must match the sole pending batch;15s timeout disconnects. Query FINAL remains authoritative. Heartbeat `{type:"health",collector,watermark,metrics,sentAt}` every5s. Invalid resume emits `reset`, closes and requires bounded rebootstrap. Native `{type:"native-candle",source:"binance-native-kline",interval,candle}` events are separate. Unknown command fields/versions rejected; maximum16 sockets,1KiB inbound commands,1MiB buffered output,4 shared queries. HTTP history admits at most3 slots, reserving one for durable execution replay; only one entire heatmap request is admitted before database/worker work. Contention returns503 with Retry-After:1.

Execution fields reuse client NormalizedExecution + receive timestamp, actual quoteNotional, original decimal strings in database, first/last underlying trade IDs. REST has no event-publication E: eventTimeMs is null, timeMs is venue execution T. aggTrade records are aggregate market executions, not orders/positions. RPI q included, insurance/ADL excluded by venue.
Bootstrap starts15m before initial startup. Connect official `/market/stream` before REST catch-up. At most10000 volatile executions,1000-record commits with250ms pacing plus insert/fsync time. Publish durable head only after insert and atomic fsynced checkpoint. Out-of-order WS records sort by aggregate ID; overlap deduplicates. Missing IDs switch to REST fromId inclusive pagination, with two retries before retaining an explicit gap. REST uses shared300ms gate, >1600 used-weight cooldown and429/418 Retry-After. Recovery retains conservative47h cutoff within documented48h horizon. Overflow reconnects and replays durable checkpoint; no silently complete coverage. Rotation23h, ws ping/pong,15s traffic watchdog, bounded30s retry with jitter. OI remains observed30s. Confirmed coverage ends exclusively at latest durable execution T, not wall-clock now.
Footprint HTTP response includes `cursor`: last execution actually included in bounded [from,to) snapshot (or watermark for an empty snapshot). Resume from cursor rather than assuming all records through watermark fit a time boundary.

Copied shared/footprint.ts is the client's pure accumulator, with only .ts import extension adapted. shared/protocol.ts supplies runtime grids/durations. Update together and compare checksums/fixtures; do not fork aggregation semantics.

